<urn:atm:triage:finding/AI33-M5-SQLITE-READER-BUDGET-EXHAUSTED>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "AI33-M5-SQLITE-READER-BUDGET-EXHAUSTED" ;
  triage:title "Admission-capacity mass-503 root cause: SQLite reader-handle budget exhausted under load" ;
  triage:description "With the response-body-capture harness repair (AI33-M5-RESPONSE-BODY-DISCARDED fix) landed, arch-ctm reran the M5 admission-capacity benchmark on branch feature/pAI-s33-admission-capacity-smoke @ 2a5d252b. The captured HTTP 503 response body is: ATM_DAEMON_UNAVAILABLE: sqlite connection budget exceeded (max 3 concurrent reader handles with one permanent writer handle). This is now confirmed real evidence (not a hypothesis) for the mass-503-rejection defect. The daemon's local admission path enforces a hard SQLite reader-handle pool ceiling of 3 concurrent readers (plus 1 permanent writer), which is far below the required >=1,000 admissions/s throughput target. Evidence artifact: artifacts/smoke/admission-capacity/admission-capacity-20260730T010411Z.json on that branch (the M5 host does not have sc-compose installed so HTML rendering of that evidence failed there; only the JSON was retained)." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-AI" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
  triage:category "correctness" ;
  triage:severity "blocking" ;
  triage:repeatable false ;
  triage:sweepScope "file_only" ;
  triage:status "fixed" ;
  triage:dispatchReady false ;
  triage:triagedAt "2026-07-30T01:05:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:foundIn triage:AICH-S13 ;
  triage:foundAt "2026-07-30T01:04:30Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/AI33-M5-SQLITE-READER-BUDGET-EXHAUSTED/AI33-M5-1> ;
  triage:progressNote "AI33-M5-READERBUDGET-QA-1 (round 2): MAX_SQLITE_READER_CONNECTIONS cap + SharedDbConnectionGuard confirmed genuinely removed (landed d61292a8, ancestor of cited fix commits 4461934a/85031365, both confirmed ancestors of branch head 67568745); regression test concurrent_read_handles_do_not_fail_fast_at_an_arbitrary_reader_cap confirmed passing. Round-1 evidence artifact was missing from disk (FAIL); arch-ctm regenerated and committed real replacement evidence at artifacts/smoke/admission-capacity/admission-capacity-20260730T024015Z.json (commit 67568745, ancestor bc866463). Independently re-parsed the JSON: 2 isolated runs x 10 intervals = 20/20 intervals with accepted_count=response_count=1000, first_failure=null (zero reader-budget 503s). Some intervals show passed:false, but that reflects the separate timing/latency criterion tracked by AI33-M5-CAPACITY-THROUGHPUT-FAIL (unaffected, stays open) -- not a reader-budget rejection. Closed by quality-mgr." ;
  triage:closedAt "2026-07-30T02:50:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:closedBy "quality-mgr" ;
  triage:triageRecordVersion "2" .

